,"219 ถนนสวนอ้อยซอยกลาง, 10300","","","","","f"],["Golden Place","supermarket",13.77919,100.51369,"","","","","","s"],["Dusit Palace (พระราชวังดุสิต)","castle",13.77264,100.51188,"","","","","","a"],["Vajiravudh College (โรงเรียนวชิราวุธวิทยาลัย)","school",13.77617,100.518,"","","","","","f"],["Dusit Palace","sight",13.77405,100.51246,"","09:30-16:00","","","","r","PERMANENTLY CLOSED! Sometimes called New Royal City, Dusit Park, Dusit Garden, or simply Dusit, is a complex of palaces and royal residences in the south of the Dusit district. The palace was established by King Rama V, the first Thai…"],["Vimanmek Mansion","sight",13.77389,100.51278,"","","","","","r","Touted as the world's largest golden teak building, this palace was the home of King Rama V in the early 20th century. It was built as a summer retreat on the island of Ko Si Chang, but was transported to Bangkok in pieces in 1901. A…"],["Abhisek Dusit Throne Hall","sight",13.77347,100.51306,"","","","","","r","Built in 1904, this beautiful hall used to be used for royal meetings and banquets. Its exterior is unique as it is clearly a mix of Victorian and Islamic influences. Home to the largest part of HM Queen Sirikit's SUPPORT Museum, it…"],["Dusit Zoo","sight",13.77436,100.51719,"71 Rama V Rd","Daily, 08:00-18:00","","","","r","The zoo is an excellent destination for families and children. It is a lush and green zoo with many flowers, trees and ponds. A fun activity is floating on the water with the foot-peddle boats, or riding the small tram, but it costs 60…"],["King Rama V Equestrian Statue","sight",13.76922,100.51203,"Uthong Nai Rd","","","","","r","The entrance to Dusit Palace is a gigantic motorway with the statue of King Rama V (Chulalongkorn) riding a stallion right in the centre. It is the first monument dedicated to a Thai king, completed in 1908 and inaugurated by King Rama…"],["Wat Benchamabophit","sight",13.76656,100.51414,"Si Ayutthaya Rd","Daily, 06:00-18:00","","","","r","The newest of Bangkok's famous temples, this unique wat was constructed during the reign of King Rama V. It employs European ecclesiastical details, such as stained glass windows, and contains a cloister collection of bronze Buddha…"],["Wat Intharawihan","sight",13.76693,100.50295,"114 Wisut Kasat Rd","Daily, 08:30-20:00","","","","r","This temple is known for the so-called Standing Buddha or Big Buddha (Luang Pho To), a 32 m high golden Buddha image. The statue is covered with 24,000 golden mosaics from Italy. The topknot of the Buddha image contains a relic of Lord…"],["Ratchadamnoen Stadium","activity",13.76096,100.50875,"Ratchadamnoen Nok Rd","Mon, Wed-Thu 18:30-22:30, Sun 17:00-20:00 and 20:30-00:00","","","","r","When the locals want entertainment, they head to the stadium for some Thai boxing. Or Muay Thai, as the Thais call it. It is very expensive though, expect to pay 1,000 baht for an outer-ring seat, 1,500 baht for a middle-ring seat and…"]]}